            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: multipartFile.getOriginalFilename() (user-controlled file input). Sink: destinationDir.toPath().resolve(...) at line 75, used to create a file handle. Dataflow: The untrusted filename is directly resolved against a base directory without sanitization. An attacker can provide a filename containing '..' path sequences (e.g., '../foo.txt') to break out of the intended user directory. Sanitization: None. Conclusion: The code is vulnerable to path traversal."
          },
