              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:The code implements an flawed authentication check using request.getMethod().equals('GET') on line 46. If the method is 'GET', it triggers an error, but any other HTTP method (e.g., POST, PUT) bypasses this check and reaches line 54, which returns a sensitive flag header. Source: HTTP request verb. Sink: line 54 (ResponseEntity builder leakage of sensitive information). Dataflow: The untrusted HTTP method directly dictates whether the logic reaches the sensitive flag return. Conclusion: This is an improper authorization vulnerability."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The code implements an flawed authentication check using request.getMethod().equals('GET') on line 46. If the method is 'GET', it triggers an error, but any other HTTP method (e.g., POST, PUT) bypasses this check and reaches line 54, which returns a sensitive flag header. Source: HTTP request verb. Sink: line 54 (ResponseEntity builder leakage of sensitive information). Dataflow: The untrusted HTTP method directly dictates whether the logic reaches the sensitive flag return. Conclusion: This is an improper authorization vulnerability."
          },
